text I don't know when it happened, but we all went our separate ways...
text Everyone went to college after graduating high school.
text Misae-san is still the dorm mother, still as busy as ever. With no reason for me to go to there though, I don't see her anymore.
text As for Furukawa Bread, I'm not all that picky about my bread, so I've stopped buying from there.
text Yoshino Yusuke is probably still doing electrical work somewhere in this town.
text I'm amazed that I ran into him so many times as a student. I stopped seeing him around town after graduating.
text Sunohara and Mei-chan returned to their family's home.
text And even though we're scattered...
text Every once in a while, I think about that one game of grass-lot baseball.
text It brings a smile to my face.
text It felt good.
text And not because of whether we won or lost.
text After smiling for a bit, my mood settles.
text This is how I restore my spirits.
text For all the days that I have ahead of me.
text Let's go.
music ~
text I stand back up.
